Answer the probes, add focus events and synchronized output, and consume strings

Fill in the calls of mode 2026, synchronized output, and mode 1004, focus
events: CSI ? 2026 h holds the screen's updates until CSI ? 2026 l, a reset
or tsm_vte_end_sync_hold(), which a renderer calls when the hold outlasts
its bound; tsm_vte_handle_focus() sends CSI I or CSI O while mode 1004 is set.

Answer the probes an application sends to learn the terminal, each in the
order it came, so that an application that ends a group of probes with DA1
knows that a probe answered before DA1 is supported:
* DA1 reports a VT220 with ANSI color, CSI ? 62 ; 22 c, and no longer the
  options the parser does not implement;
* CPR and DECXCPR, CSI 6 n and CSI ? 6 n, count the row from the top margin
  in origin mode and report the last column for a cursor waiting to wrap;
* XTVERSION, CSI > q and CSI > 0 q, answers DCS > | libtsm(VERSION) ST,
  where it set the LEDs as DECLL;
* DECRQM, CSI Ps $ p and CSI ? Ps $ p, answers CSI Ps ; Pm $ y for every
  mode the parser takes, the modes it ignores as fixed, and mode 2027,
  grapheme clustering, as not recognized;
* OSC 10 and 11 answer only the exact queries "10;?" and "11;?".
DECLL now takes only CSI Ps q and DECSCUSR only CSI Ps SP q, and CSI > p,
xterm's pointer mode, is ignored instead of resetting the terminal.

The OSC buffer, 128 bytes, grows as a string needs up to 2 MiB, which holds
OSC 52 with 1 MiB of text in base64, and is freed after a long string. OSC 52
goes to the clipboard callback when one is set, with its targets and its
payload. A string longer than the buffer is consumed and dropped, where before
it was cut short and dispatched; one that CAN, SUB or a C1 control other than
ST ends is cancelled. Clearing a sequence's state no longer clears the buffer.
DCS, SOS, PM and APC strings are consumed without effect, as before.

